# Anime Recommender

A content-based anime recommendation system built with Python, Flask, React, TF-IDF, K-Nearest Neighbors, and the Jikan API. The system generates personalized recommendations using anime genres, synopsis text, ratings, and popularity data.

Live Demo: 
https://anime-recommender-coral.vercel.app/
*Note: Initial requests may take up to 50 seconds due to Render backend cold starts.*

## Highlights

- Content-Based Recommendation Engine using TF-IDF vectorization and KNN similarity search
- Hybrid Ranking System combining content similarity, community ratings, and popularity scores
- Franchise Deduplication to prevent sequels, movies, and alternate versions from dominating results
- Dynamic Anime Metadata retrieval through the Jikan API
- Interactive React Frontend with filtering by genre, score, and episode count
- Cloud Deployment using Render (backend) and Vercel (frontend)

## Technologies

- Python
- Flask
- Scikit-Learn
- Pandas
- React
- JavaScript
- Jikan API
- Render
- Vercel

## How It Works

1. User searches for an anime title.
2. TF-IDF vectorization converts anime genres and synopsis text into feature vectors.
3. K-Nearest Neighbors identifies the most similar anime based on cosine similarity.
4. A hybrid ranking formula combines:
   - Content similarity
   - Anime rating score
   - Popularity score
5. Franchise and sequel filtering removes redundant recommendations.
6. Results are returned to the React frontend and displayed with similarity explanations and metadata.

## Features

- Anime title autocomplete search
- Recommendation explanations
- Genre filtering
- Score filtering
- Episode count filtering
- Popularity-aware ranking
- Franchise deduplication
